PREDICATION NOT PREDICTION!!

It is what Itanium and ARM does add an extra register to every instruction as data dependency. For instructions that 
can execute unconditionally a common register with a value of 1 is used.

Long story short compiler does an if-conversion to convert control dependencies to data dependencies. How? By making
the conditional statement store its result into a register and adding a data dependency on this register on all
branch instructions.

Now you can do what Thumb-2 seems to do viz., instead of predicating every instruction you can create a set of 4 instruction
packet and apply predicate to that.

Anyways the fake data dependency is to prevent the reordering and the register value can be used to either to execute 
or not execute the instruction. Instead of noop execution one can execute blindly but not do a commit conditionally 
depending upon whether the processor has a ROB or not.

